        "file": "drivers/raw/ntb/ntb.c",
        "start_line": 140,
        "end_line": 141,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "medium",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Unchecked rte_zmalloc and peer_mw_cnt/mw_cnt mismatch; leak on repeat",
        "explanation": "peer_mw_size is allocated with peer_mw_cnt entries (from peer spad) and may be NULL, but the loop indexes it up to local hw->mw_cnt. If the peer count is smaller or the allocation fails, this is an out-of-bounds write or NULL dereference. It is also never freed and is reallocated each time the peer comes up again, so it leaks.",
        "suggestion": "Check the allocation result, bound the loop by min(mw_cnt, peer_mw_cnt) or allocate mw_cnt entries, and free peer_mw_size on peer down and on close.",
        "evidence": "hw->peer_mw_size = rte_zmalloc(\"uint64_t\",\n\t\t\t\t   hw->peer_mw_cnt * sizeof(uint64_t), 0);",
        "confidence": 0.6,
        "id": "84c0e33ac011",
        "hunk_id": "drivers/raw/ntb/ntb.c#1",
        "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
        "tier": 3,
        "escalated_from": [],
        "also_reported_by": []
      },
      {
        "file": "drivers/raw/ntb/ntb.c",
        "start_line": 333,
        "end_line": 334,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "medium",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "hw->mz allocation unchecked and never freed; leaks on restart or error",
        "explanation": "rte_zmalloc is unchecked, and hw->mz is neither freed on error return, nor in stop or close. Each start leaks the array. The memzones are also never freed. ntb_set_mw returns early when a memzone already exists without setting hw->mz[mw_idx], so after a restart the array entry stays NULL.",
        "suggestion": "Check for NULL, free hw->mz on failure and in stop/close, and free the memzones on stop.",
        "evidence": "hw->mz = rte_zmalloc(\"struct rte_memzone *\",",
        "confidence": 0.55,
        "id": "24438ace2e39",
        "hunk_id": "drivers/raw/ntb/ntb.c#2",
        "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
        "tier": 3,
        "escalated_from": [],
        "also_reported_by": []
      },
      {
        "file": "drivers/raw/ntb/ntb.c",
        "start_line": 639,
        "end_line": 644,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "medium",
        "category": "error-handling",
        "title": "Interrupt callback left registered on init failure paths",
        "explanation": "The callback is registered, and then there are many error returns. ntb_create releases the rawdev on failure, but the callback still points at the freed dev. A later interrupt would use freed memory. The return value of rte_intr_callback_register is also ignored.",
        "suggestion": "Check the register result, and on failure unregister the callback and disable efd before returning.",
        "evidence": "rte_intr_callback_register(intr_handle,\n\t\t\t\t   ntb_dev_intr_handler, dev);",
        "confidence": 0.55,
        "id": "3b4cc7121bcb",
        "hunk_id": "drivers/raw/ntb/ntb.c#6",
        "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
        "tier": 3,
        "escalated_from": [],
        "also_reported_by": []
      },
      {
        "file": "drivers/raw/ntb/ntb.c",
        "start_line": 63,
        "end_line": 67,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "low",
        "category": "error-handling",
        "title": "Memzone not freed when mw_set_trans fails",
        "explanation": "If mw_set_trans fails, the reserved memzone stays reserved and is stored in hw->mz. A later retry finds it via rte_memzone_lookup and returns 0 without ever setting the translation.",
        "suggestion": "Call rte_memzone_free(mz) and clear hw->mz[mw_idx] on failure.",
        "evidence": "ret = (*hw->ntb_ops->mw_set_trans)(dev, mw_idx, mz->iova, mw_size);",
